   "line": [
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight to c3 is a springboard into many systems — you'll know it as the Grand Prix introduction, but it's also a sly move order, because next move the other knight can come out and transpose straight back into an Open Sicilian. So how you answer it depends entirely on which Sicilian you play."
  },
  {
   "ply": 4,
   "t": 59.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/1p1ppppp/p7/2p5/4P3/2N5/PPPP1PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 3",
   "line": [
    "a6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The underrated reply is an early a6 — most reach for a knight or a central pawn, but a6 makes wonderful sense for a Najdorf player and is a fine way to meet the Closed Sicilian and the Grand Prix alike.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 5,
   "t": 70,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/1p1ppppp/p7/2p5/4P3/2N3P1/PPPP1P1P/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 3",
   "line": [
    "g3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 78,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/3ppppp/p7/1pp5/4P3/2N3P1/PPPP1P1P/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The whole point of a6 is a quick b5 — grabbing queenside space early and, just as importantly, handing the light-squared bishop a natural home on the long diagonal.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 84,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/3ppppp/p7/1pp5/4P3/P1N3P1/1PPP1P1P/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "a3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 86,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b1ppppp/p7/1pp5/4P3/P1N3P1/1PPP1P1P/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Bb7"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 91,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b1ppppp/p7/1pp5/4P3/P1N3P1/1PPP1PBP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 2 5",
   "line": [
    "Bg2"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now the classic Sicilian setup: the central pawns settle on d6 and e6, a Scheveningen-style shell that controls a cluster of key squares. It looks passive but it's the heart and soul of the opening — and the knight can come out to f6 without fear, since the central break just runs into a loose bishop.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 144.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b2pppp/p2p4/1pp5/4P3/P1N3P1/1PPP1PBP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "d6"
   ],
   "spoken": "d6 gives maximum flexibility and, crucially, opens a d7 square for the other knight — in these structures it belongs there rather than on c6, where it would clumsily block the fianchettoed bishop.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 158,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b2pppp/p2p4/1pp5/4P3/P1NP2P1/1PP2PBP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 0 6",
