   "fen": "r3k2r/2q1bpp1/p2ppP2/2n3Np/P4P2/2Pp2PP/4N1K1/R1BQ1R2 b kq - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "exf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Of the remaining captures, the pawn recapture keeps the centre intact and stays a pawn up, and the pawn mass shields the king while the opponent's own shelter is far more exposed with the g-file about to open.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 748.5,
   "fen": "r3k2r/2q1bpp1/p2ppP2/2n3Np/P4P2/2P3PP/4p1K1/R1BQ1R2 w kq - 0 19",
   "line": [
    "dxe2"
   ],
   "spoken": "Recapturing toward the centre with the pawn is counter-intuitive but correct — in the Sicilian, keeping pawns pristine is rarely the priority. Shifting a pawn onto the f-file actually improves the structure: more pawns mean a safer king, it pries open the g-file as a direct road to the enemy king, and the front doubled pawn becomes a free battering ram to push while the one behind guards home. And it sets up the e4 outpost, the crown of the whole plan.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
