    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The pawn to d5 does three jobs at once — it cements the monster knight, springs the queen to life, and adds a third attacker to the target. And once you're this far ahead, remember the value of simplification: trading eliminates calculation, and don't fret about conceding a passed rook-pawn — it's a marathon from promotion while the centre steamrolls. In the technical phase, a pawn can even be used to cut the enemy bishop off a key square near the queening line.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
