   "line": [],
   "spoken": "In practice the knight to c3 usually isn't followed by the transposing knight move at all — far more often it's the Closed Sicilian with a kingside fianchetto, or the Grand Prix Attack with the f-pawn. Either way, the lesson stands: have a prepared line against the early knight to c3.",
